      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Increasing border security and enforcing stricter immigration policies effectively prevents crime, terrorism, and exploitation by unauthorized employers, as irregular migration allows these threats to enter without oversight. There is no doubt that these measures create greater national safety, yet they also succeed in preserving cultural and economic diversity by ensuring that massive numbers of skilled workers can enter legally for their work.\n\nWhile proponents of strict enforcement often cite the disruption to families, this is outweighed by the fact that proper vetting and security protocols are designed to build those relationships more robustly. Strengthening borders and better enforcing regulations ensures that the United States remains a place where every citizen, legal or not, can thrive. These measures are not just about exclusion; they are about creating a system where individuals can flourish through legalization, family reunification, and economic stability under a fair and transparent framework.",
